    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">50 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Interview Hub</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">SDE-1 / SDE-2 / SDE-3</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Data: Jan 2024 - Nov 2026</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Recently asked coding questions (2024-26)</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Which problems do candidates actually report from Meta, Amazon, Microsoft, Google, Flipkart, Walmart and Uber coding rounds? This page reads 1,883 question reports pulled from 955 public interview-experience posts, ranks the most reported problems, splits them by company, level and round type, shows how often the problem came back as a variant, and turns the result into a practice plan with two templates that cover the top of the list.</p>\r\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Before this page:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-start-here\">How coding rounds work</a> and <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-sheets-guide\">Problem sheets guide</a>. <b>Pairs well with:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-testing-your-code\">Testing your code in the interview</a> and <a href=\"{{BASE}}coding/coding-revision-system\">Revision system</a>.</p>\r\n"
